  "body": {
    "id": "lem:violated-row-mahalanobis-separation",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(\\Sigma_0=\\Sigma_0'\\succ0\\), let \\(P_{v,b}^0=\\{g:A_{v,b}^0g\\le b_{v,b}^0\\}\\), let \\(u_*\\in\\mathbb R^d\\), and suppose row \\(i\\) has gap\n\\[\n \\gamma=(A_{v,b}^0u_*-b_{v,b}^0)_i>0.\n\\]\nIf \\(s\\ge\\|(A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}\\|_{\\Sigma_0}>0\\), then\n\\[\n \\inf_{g\\in P_{v,b}^0}\\|u_*-g\\|_{\\Sigma_0^{-1}}\n \\ge \\frac{\\gamma}{s}>0.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "PvbZero",
      "AvecZero",
      "bvecZero",
      "uStarZero",
      "SigmaZero",
      "d"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:job-corps-radius-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(g\\in P_{v,b}^0\\).  Component feasibility gives \\((A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}g\\le(b_{v,b}^0)_i\\); hence\n\\[\n \\gamma\n \\le (A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}(u_*-g). \\tag{21}\n\\]\nApply Cauchy--Schwarz after inserting \\(\\Sigma_0^{1/2}\\Sigma_0^{-1/2}\\):\n\\[\n \\begin{aligned}\n (A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}(u_*-g)\n &=\\{(A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}\\Sigma_0^{1/2}\\}\n   \\{\\Sigma_0^{-1/2}(u_*-g)\\}\\\\\n &\\le \\|(A_{v,b}^0)_{i\\cdot}\\|_{\\Sigma_0}\n       \\|u_*-g\\|_{\\Sigma_0^{-1}}\n \\le s\\|u_*-g\\|_{\\Sigma_0^{-1}}.\n \\end{aligned} \\tag{22}\n\\]\nPositive definiteness of \\(\\Sigma_0\\) and \\(\\gamma>0\\) imply that the selected row is nonzero and hence that its \\(\\Sigma_0\\)-norm is positive.  Divide (21)--(22) by \\(s>0\\) and take the infimum over \\(g\\in P_{v,b}^0\\).",
    "proof_basis": {
